[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":1321},["ShallowReactive",2],{"article-ai-pattern-selection-in-fabric":3,"articles-100":1141,"topic-of-article-ai-pattern-selection-in-fabric":1283,"articles-10":1300},{"id":4,"title":5,"alt":6,"body":7,"description":1127,"extension":1128,"image":1129,"meta":1130,"navigation":213,"path":1131,"postDate":1132,"published":1133,"seo":1134,"stem":1135,"tags":1136,"topic":1138,"updated":1139,"url":1139,"__hash__":1140},"blog\u002Fblog\u002Fai-pattern-selection-in-fabric.md","fzf + fabric: Smart selection for LLM patterns and models","AI Pattern Selection in Fabric",{"type":8,"value":9,"toc":1121},"minimark",[10,22,25,30,44,73,84,98,101,1047,1056,1060,1063,1083,1086,1090,1093,1096,1104,1107,1111,1114,1117],[11,12,13,14,21],"p",{},"I have been using ",[15,16,20],"a",{"href":17,"rel":18},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fdanielmiessler\u002Ffabric",[19],"nofollow","fabric"," to run LLM prompts on text. It's like having a Swiss Army knife of LLM tools. You feed it text, and it helps analyze it in different ways. With 31k+ GitHub stars, lots of people find it useful.",[11,23,24],{},"But here's the thing: there were too many patterns available. I kept staring at my screen trying to remember how they are named. Plus, I wanted to have the flexibility to choose different LLM models without having to memorize their names.",[26,27,29],"h2",{"id":28},"the-solution","The solution",[11,31,32,33,38,39,43],{},"I used ",[15,34,37],{"href":35,"rel":36},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fjunegunn\u002Ffzf",[19],"fzf",", a fuzzy finder tool I also use for ",[15,40,42],{"href":41},"\u002Fblog\u002Fgit-and-command-line-next-level-workflow\u002F","checking out Git branches",", to create searchable menus for fabric. Instead of memorizing commands, I just:",[45,46,47,51,70],"ol",{},[48,49,50],"li",{},"Send text to fabric",[48,52,53,54],{},"Type any parts of what I want. fzf is smart about matching:\n",[55,56,57,64],"ul",{},[48,58,59,63],{},[60,61,62],"code",{},"xwis"," finds \"extract_wisdom\"",[48,65,66,69],{},[60,67,68],{},"sumtext"," matches \"summarize_text\"",[48,71,72],{},"Press enter to run",[11,74,75,76,79,80,83],{},"The magic happens with two shell commands (add to ",[60,77,78],{},".zshrc"," or ",[60,81,82],{},".bashrc","):",[55,85,86,92],{},[48,87,88,91],{},[60,89,90],{},"fp"," - Pick a pattern with fuzzy search",[48,93,94,97],{},[60,95,96],{},"fps"," - Same smart matching, but for both model and pattern",[11,99,100],{},"Here's the code that makes it work:",[102,103,108],"pre",{"className":104,"code":105,"language":106,"meta":107,"style":107},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","# Fabric CLI Helper Functions\n# Interactive selection of models and patterns for fabric AI tool\n# Requirements: fabric(https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fdanielmiessler\u002Ffabric), fzf(https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fjunegunn\u002Ffzf)\n#\n# Usage Examples:\n#   Model + Pattern Selection (fps alias):\n#     fps -u \u003Curl>                    # Process URL content\n#     pbpaste | fps                   # Process clipboard content\n#     yt \u003Cyoutube_url> | fps          # Process YouTube transcript\n#     echo \"text\" | fps               # Process any text content\n#\n#   Pattern Selection Only (fp alias):\n#     fp -u \u003Curl>                     # Use default model with URL\n#     pbpaste | fp                    # Use default model with clipboard\n#     yt \u003Cyoutube_url> | fp           # Use default model with transcript\n#     cat file.txt | fp               # Process any text content\n\n# Handle stdin input for fabric functions\n_fabric_handle_input() {\n  if [ -t 0 ]; then\n    return 1  # No stdin\n  else\n    cat       # Return stdin content\n    return 0\n  fi\n}\n\n# Select a pattern using fzf\n_fabric_select_pattern() {\n  fabric -l | fzf --height 40% --border --ansi --prompt=\"Select pattern: \"\n}\n\n# Select and run fabric with a pattern\n# Usage: fabric_with_pattern [additional_args...]\nfabric_with_pattern() {\n  local input=\"\"\n  local has_stdin=0\n\n  if input=$(_fabric_handle_input); then\n    has_stdin=1\n  fi\n\n  local pattern=$(_fabric_select_pattern)\n  [ -z \"$pattern\" ] && { echo \"No pattern selected.\"; return 1; }\n\n  if [ $has_stdin -eq 1 ]; then\n    echo \"$input\" | fabric --pattern \"$pattern\" \"$@\"\n  else\n    fabric --pattern \"$pattern\" \"$@\"\n  fi\n}\n\n# Select and run fabric with both model and pattern\n# Usage: fabric_with_model_pattern [additional_args...]\nfabric_with_model_pattern() {\n  local input=\"\"\n  local has_stdin=0\n\n  if input=$(_fabric_handle_input); then\n    has_stdin=1\n  fi\n\n  local model_line=$(fabric -L | fzf --height 40% --border --ansi --prompt=\"Select model: \")\n  [ -z \"$model_line\" ] && { echo \"No model selected.\"; return 1; }\n\n  local model=$(echo \"$model_line\" | sed -E 's\u002F.*[[:space:]]([^[:space:]]+)$\u002F\\1\u002F')\n\n  local pattern=$(_fabric_select_pattern)\n  [ -z \"$pattern\" ] && { echo \"No pattern selected.\"; return 1; }\n\n  if [ $has_stdin -eq 1 ]; then\n    echo \"$input\" | fabric --model \"$model\" --pattern \"$pattern\" \"$@\"\n  else\n    fabric --model \"$model\" --pattern \"$pattern\" \"$@\"\n  fi\n}\n\n# Get YouTube transcript with fabric\n# Usage: yt \u003Cvideo_link>\nyt() {\n  local video_link=\"$1\"\n  fabric -y \"$video_link\" --transcript\n}\n\n# Aliases for convenience\nalias fp='fabric_with_pattern'\nalias fps='fabric_with_model_pattern'\n","bash","",[60,109,110,119,125,131,137,143,149,155,161,167,173,178,184,190,196,202,208,215,221,232,255,267,273,282,290,296,302,307,313,321,355,360,365,371,377,385,400,413,418,437,448,453,458,475,513,518,535,570,575,595,600,605,610,616,622,630,641,652,657,674,683,688,693,729,758,763,796,801,816,843,848,863,902,907,934,939,944,949,955,961,969,986,1004,1009,1014,1020,1034],{"__ignoreMap":107},[111,112,115],"span",{"class":113,"line":114},"line",1,[111,116,118],{"class":117},"sJ8bj","# Fabric CLI Helper Functions\n"