ass":341},[111,1002,1003],{"class":247}," --transcript\n",[111,1005,1007],{"class":113,"line":1006},83,[111,1008,301],{"class":230},[111,1010,1012],{"class":113,"line":1011},84,[111,1013,214],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":213},[111,1015,1017],{"class":113,"line":1016},85,[111,1018,1019],{"class":117},"# Aliases for convenience\n",[111,1021,1023,1026,1029,1031],{"class":113,"line":1022},86,[111,1024,1025],{"class":237},"alias",[111,1027,1028],{"class":230}," fp",[111,1030,396],{"class":237},[111,1032,1033],{"class":341},"'fabric_with_pattern'\n",[111,1035,1037,1039,1042,1044],{"class":113,"line":1036},87,[111,1038,1025],{"class":237},[111,1040,1041],{"class":230}," fps",[111,1043,396],{"class":237},[111,1045,1046],{"class":341},"'fabric_with_model_pattern'\n",[11,1048,1049,1050,1055],{},"Also available on ",[15,1051,1054],{"href":1052,"rel":1053},"https:\u002F\u002Fgist.github.com\u002FSubodhDahal\u002F38436348aedf0596e48d17ffcffa7d51",[19],"GitHub Gist",".",[26,1057,1059],{"id":1058},"using-it-day-to-day","Using It Day-to-Day",[11,1061,1062],{},"It's as simple as:",[55,1064,1065,1071,1077],{},[48,1066,1067,1070],{},[60,1068,1069],{},"fp -u example.com"," to analyze a website",[48,1072,1073,1076],{},[60,1074,1075],{},"pbpaste | fp"," to analyze clipboard content",[48,1078,1079,1082],{},[60,1080,1081],{},"cat file.txt | fps"," to analyze a file with a specific model",[11,1084,1085],{},"The menu pops up, you pick what you want, and fabric does the rest.",[26,1087,1089],{"id":1088},"making-it-work-for-you","Making It Work for You",[11,1091,1092],{},"You know how your phone probably has dozens of apps, but you only use a handful regularly? It's the same with fabric patterns. While having options is great, too many choices can slow you down.",[11,1094,1095],{},"I cleaned up my pattern collection by:",[55,1097,1098,1101],{},[48,1099,1100],{},"Keeping only the patterns I actually use",[48,1102,1103],{},"Tweaking the remaining ones to work exactly how I want",[11,1105,1106],{},"Since patterns are just markdown files, changing them is as easy as editing a text file.",[26,1108,1110],{"id":1109},"why-this-matters","Why This Matters",[11,1112,1113],{},"I'm not reinventing the wheel here. These are just small tweaks that make fabric feel more natural to use. But sometimes that's all you need: tools that work the way your brain works.",[11,1115,1116],{},"Before, I'd hesitate to use fabric because remembering all the commands felt like work. Now? It's just copy, paste, pick, and done. If you use fabric, give these helpers a try.",[1118,1119,1120],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sJ8bj, html code.shiki .sJ8bj{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D}html pre.shiki code .sScJk, html code.shiki .sScJk{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .sVt8B, html code.shiki .sVt8B{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .szBVR, html code.shiki .szBVR{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583}html pre.shiki code .sj4cs, html code.shiki .sj4cs{--shiki-default:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF}html pre.shiki code .sZZnC, html code.shiki .sZZnC{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html.dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}",{"title":107,"searchDepth":121,"depth":121,"links":1122},[1123,1124,1125,1126],{"id":28,"depth":121,"text":29},{"id":1058,"depth":121,"text":1059},{"id":1088,"depth":121,"text":1089},{"id":1109,"depth":121,"text":1110},"Enhance your experience with fabric, the AI prompt tool, by using interactive selection for patterns and models.","md","\u002Fimages\u002Ffabric-ai-pattern-selection.webp",{},"\u002Fblog\u002Fai-pattern-selection-in-fabric","2025-05-24",false,{"title":5,"description":1127},"blog\u002Fai-pattern-selection-in-fabric",[1137],"developer productivity","command-line",null,"oQ71q-pYSq1qZlt7N4OdmQ5_Ey7tGty6RprKjvW8XmE",[1142,1152,1162,1173,1182,1193,1202,1208,1215,1224,1233,1241,1243,1249,1257,1264,1270,1277],{"title":1143,"description":1144,"tags":1145,"postDate":1150,"path":1151,"url":1139,"topic":1146},"Why I let AI agents change my OS only through Nix","AI agents make it trivial to change your operating system and hard to remember what they changed. Here's why I manage NixOS and macOS from one Nix config in Git.",[1146,1147,1148,1149,1137],"nixos","nix","nix-darwin","ai","2026-11-26","\u002Fblog\u002Fconfiguring-my-os-with-nix-in-the-age-of-ai",{"title":1153,"description":1154,"tags":1155,"postDate":1159,"path":1160,"url":1139,"topic":1161},"A browser tool that puts every carousel photo on the same white mat, like a gallery print","Instagram can keep each photo's original aspect ratio in a carousel, but I prefer a white canvas with even borders. I built a page that pads every image onto one shared canvas, entirely in the browser.",[1156,1157,1158],"tools","instagram","photography","2026-11-25","\u002Fblog\u002Finstagram-carousel-padding-tool","hiking-photography",{"title":1163,"description":1164,"tags":1165,"postDate":1171,"path":1172,"url":1139,"topic":1146},"Getting Handy speech-to-text to type on NixOS and COSMIC, and to use my eGPU","Handy's shortcut did nothing, and after I fixed that, nothing got typed. A Wayland shortcut, a microphone, the paste method and an autostart file caused it, and the GPU did not.",[1166,1146,1167,1168,1169,1170],"troubleshooting","cosmic","wayland","speech-to-text","egpu","2026-11-19","\u002Fblog\u002Fhandy-speech-to-text-nixos-cosmic-egpu",{"title":1174,"description":1175,"tags":1176,"postDate":1180,"path":1181,"url":1139,"topic":1146},"Getting a Razer Core X eGPU to work after login on NixOS, without timing the boot","My Razer Core X eGPU only worked if I timed it against boot. On NixOS the NVIDIA driver rejected the hotplugged card; PCI kernel parameters and a device node fixed it.",[1166,1146,1170,1177,1178,1179],"thunderbolt","nvidia","linux","2026-11-18","\u002Fblog\u002Frazer-core-x-egpu-hotplug-nixos",{"title":1183,"description":1184,"tags":1185,"postDate":1191,"path":1192,"url":1139,"topic":1138},"Stop stashing half-finished work: use Git worktrees and Worktrunk","Git worktrees keep separate branches checked out at once. Worktrunk automates per-worktree setup. The same isolation also works for parallel AI agents.",[1186,1187,1188,1137,1189,1190],"git","worktrees","worktrunk","command line","workflow","2026-08-16","\u002Fblog\u002Fworktrees-with-worktrunk",{"title":1194,"description":1195,"tags":1196,"postDate":1200,"path":1201,"url":1139,"topic":1199},"Self-Hosting my Git forge with Forgejo","Why I moved away from GitHub and chose a lightweight, community-driven alternative",[1197,1198,1199,1190],"homelab","open source","self-hosting","2026-04-29","\u002Fblog\u002Fself-hosting-my-git-forge",{"title":1203,"description":1204,"tags":1205,"postDate":1206,"path":1207,"url":1139,"topic":1199},"Curating my own reading and discovery feed with RSS","Taking concrete steps away from algorithms using FreshRSS, self-hosted tools, and a pipeline built for me.",[1197,1198,1199,1190],"2026-02-08","\u002Fblog\u002Freading-and-discovery-feed-curation",{"title":1209,"description":1210,"tags":1211,"postDate":1213,"path":1214,"url":1139,"topic":1199},"Fixing my broken Docker Immich+Traefik setup","Photo indexing failed in my Immich+Traefik setup. I'd misconfigured my Docker networking. Here's how I figured it out and what I changed.",[1197,1212],"networking","2025-10-31","\u002Fblog\u002Ffixing-docker-immich-traefik-setup",{"title":1216,"description":1217,"tags":1218,"postDate":1222,"path":1223,"url":1139,"topic":1138},"Quickly outline large JSON responses with a custom jq function","Use jq to automatically map and visualize the structure of large JSON responses, perfect for exploring undocumented endpoints.",[1219,1220,1189,1221,1137],"jq","json","automation","2025-10-19","\u002Fblog\u002Fjq-json-outline",{"title":1225,"description":1226,"tags":1227,"postDate":1231,"path":1232,"url":1139,"topic":1199},"Why I added RSS feeds to my blog (and how I did it in Nuxt 3)","How I built RSS and Atom feed support for my Nuxt 3 website to let readers follow my content without social media algorithms.",[1228,1229,1230],"nuxt","web development","tutorial","2025-08-31","\u002Fblog\u002Fsetting-up-rss-atom-feeds-nuxt3",{"title":1234,"description":1235,"tags":1236,"postDate":1239,"path":1240,"url":1139,"topic":1138},"Revisiting my Stream Deck for music control","How I turned my neglected Stream Deck into a useful tool for controlling YouTube Music without breaking my workflow.",[1237,1137,1221,1238],"productivity","home-office","2025-06-07","\u002Fblog\u002Fstream-deck-youtube-music",{"title":5,"description":1127,"tags":1242,"postDate":1132,"path":1131,"url":1139,"topic":1138},[1137],{"title":1244,"description":1245,"tags":1246,"postDate":1247,"path":1248,"url":1139,"topic":1138},"Effortless configuration syncing with GNU Stow and Git: a software engineer's workflow","Use GNU Stow and Git to keep config files in sync across Linux and macOS. Keep them in one repo with full history, and set up new machines in minutes.",[1137],"2025-01-12","\u002Fblog\u002Feffortless-configuration-syncing-with-gnu-stow",{"title":1250,"description":1251,"tags":1252,"postDate":1255,"path":1256,"url":1139,"topic":1161},"My 2023 travels: A visual journey","Looking back at the best pictures from my travel adventures in 2023",[1253,1254,1158],"personal","travel","2024-01-01","\u002Fblog\u002F2023-travels-visual-journey",{"title":1258,"description":1259,"tags":1260,"postDate":1262,"path":1263,"url":1139,"topic":1199},"Re-living memories through proper media organization","Organizing media such as photos and videos can bring back cherished memories and help relive them. Here's my approach to organizing my digital media collection.",[1253,1261],"technology","2023-02-06","\u002Fblog\u002Freliving-memories-through-proper-media-organization",{"title":1265,"description":1266,"tags":1267,"postDate":1268,"path":1269,"url":1139,"topic":1161},"Looking back: My 2022 in review","From new adventures and memories to lessons learned and personal growth, this year has been a year of discovery. Here's my 2022 in review.",[1253,1254],"2022-12-31","\u002Fblog\u002F2022-in-review",{"title":1271,"description":1272,"tags":1273,"postDate":1275,"path":1276,"url":1139,"topic":1138},"Git and the command-line: Take your workflow to the next level","Some tips on how to improve your Git productivity using the command-line",[1274,1137],"programming","2022-12-18","\u002Fblog\u002Fgit-and-command-line-next-level-workflow",{"title":1278,"description":1279,"tags":1280,"postDate":1281,"path":1282,"url":1139,"topic":1161},"Hiking Tsho-Rolpa lake trail in Nepal","Details of my hiking journey to the Tsho-Rolpa glacial lake in Nepal 🇳🇵, situated at 4,580m from sea level",[1254],"2022-01-22","\u002Fblog\u002Fhiking-tsho-rolpa-lake-trail-in-nepal",{"id":1284,"title":1285,"body":1286,"description":1293,"extension":1128,"meta":1294,"navigation":213,"order":1295,"path":1296,"seo":1297,"stem":1298,"__hash__":1299},"topics\u002Ftopics\u002Fcommand-line.md","Command line and developer workflow",{"type":8,"value":1287,"toc":1291},[1288],[11,1289,1